{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|status|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|statut|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|LL.|en}} {{term|statutum||a statute|lang=la}}, neuter singular of {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|statutus|lang=la}}, past participle of {{term|statuo|statuō|I set up, establish|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈstætʃuːt/}}, {{X-SAMPA|/"st{tSu:t/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Written law, as laid down by the [[legislature]].
# {{context|legal|lang=en}} (Common law) Legislated rule of [[society]] which has been given the force of law by those it governs.

